WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.706
Simulation testing

00:00:01.517 --> 00:00:02.319
isn't just for

00:00:02.131 --> 00:00:03.687
distributed databases

00:00:04.206 --> 00:00:05.774
Deterministic simulation

00:00:05.586 --> 00:00:06.894
testing is usually

00:00:06.706 --> 00:00:07.543
seen as a

00:00:07.355 --> 00:00:08.710
tool for distributed

00:00:08.522 --> 00:00:09.300
systems

00:00:09.439 --> 00:00:10.806
This essay argues

00:00:10.689 --> 00:00:11.950
every application can

00:00:11.762 --> 00:00:12.387
use it

00:00:12.910 --> 00:00:13.770
It starts with

00:00:13.582 --> 00:00:14.572
why we test

00:00:14.596 --> 00:00:15.421
reactively

00:00:15.493 --> 00:00:16.365
to pin down

00:00:16.176 --> 00:00:17.532
bugs users find

00:00:17.544 --> 00:00:18.664
and defensively

00:00:18.735 --> 00:00:19.643
to remove the

00:00:19.455 --> 00:00:20.669
doubt that slows

00:00:20.528 --> 00:00:21.565
every change

00:00:22.094 --> 00:00:23.025
Running your app

00:00:22.849 --> 00:00:24.075
inside a seedable

00:00:24.110 --> 00:00:25.643
deterministic simulation

00:00:25.455 --> 00:00:26.469
of its environment

00:00:26.292 --> 00:00:28.214
makes failures reproducible

00:00:28.026 --> 00:00:29.216
and covers far

00:00:29.028 --> 00:00:30.148
more cases than

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:31.244
hand-written tests

00:00:31.384 --> 00:00:32.480
The author's point

00:00:32.669 --> 00:00:33.553
this works for

00:00:33.459 --> 00:00:34.178
any kind of

00:00:33.990 --> 00:00:34.720
software

00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:36.242
not just databases

00:00:36.774 --> 00:00:37.788
Full story on

00:00:37.599 --> 00:00:38.495
the dashboard
